From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:03:31 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: arm: pmu: Use one compatible per SoC for M4 Pro
 and A18 Pro

The E and P cores of the T6040 (M4 Pro) and T8140 (A18 Pro) share one
PMU event encoding and counter layout, so a single PMU instance covers
both clusters. Replace the per-cluster brava/tahiti compatibles with
apple,t6040-pmu and apple,t8140-pmu.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 311c08659da794efdee06af350488406af76ea59)
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/pmu.yaml | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/pmu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/pmu.yaml
index 8771431681..b0bdbf5fdc 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/pmu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/pmu.yaml
@@ -22,12 +22,10 @@ properties:
           - apm,potenza-pmu
           - apple,avalanche-pmu
           - apple,blizzard-pmu
-          - apple,brava-e-pmu
-          - apple,brava-p-pmu
           - apple,firestorm-pmu
           - apple,icestorm-pmu
-          - apple,tahiti-e-pmu
-          - apple,tahiti-p-pmu
+          - apple,t6040-pmu
+          - apple,t8140-pmu
           - arm,armv8-pmuv3 # Only for s/w models
           - arm,arm1136-pmu
           - arm,arm1176-pmu
